  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 27,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/bf2d469148d1639816b0ac076fe8e9e19ddab34e/.github%2FFOLDER_README.md",
      "changes": 27,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/.github%2FFOLDER_README.md?ref=bf2d469148d1639816b0ac076fe8e9e19ddab34e",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": ".github/FOLDER_README.md",
      "patch": "@@ -75,5 +75,32 @@ Set a cooldown deliberately: `0` lets the holder run PR-head code on the\n self-hosted GPU runners, and raising it above `0` takes that away again along\n with their rate-limit waiver.\n \n+## DCO check\n+\n+`workflows/dco-check.yml` checks every non-merge commit introduced by a pull\n+request for a `Signed-off-by` trailer. Sign off contributions you can certify\n+under the [Developer Certificate of Origin](https://developercertificate.org/)\n+with `git commit -s`:\n+\n+```text\n+Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>\n+```\n+\n+To add a missing sign-off to your latest commit:\n+\n+```bash\n+git commit --amend --no-edit --signoff\n+git push --force-with-lease\n+```\n+\n+For multiple commits you can certify, use `git rebase --signoff HEAD~N`, replacing\n+`N` with the number of commits to update, then `git push --force-with-lease`.\n+The workflow checks the trailer format, not the signer's identity. Merge commits\n+are exempt; bot-authored non-merge commits follow the same rule as other commits.\n+\n+To require this check before merging, repository maintainers must add\n+`Developer Certificate of Origin` to the required status checks in the branch\n+protection rule or ruleset after the workflow has run.\n+\n ## Others\n - `MAINTAINER.md` defines the code maintenance model.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/bf2d469148d1639816b0ac076fe8e9e19ddab34e/.github%2FFOLDER_README.md",
      "sha": "1cf15d23482aec2769e0aad127a2b612bb59248b",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 1,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/bf2d469148d1639816b0ac076fe8e9e19ddab34e/.github%2Fpull_request_template.md",
      "changes": 1,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/.github%2Fpull_request_template.md?ref=bf2d469148d1639816b0ac076fe8e9e19ddab34e",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": ".github/pull_request_template.md",
      "patch": "@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ Examples: [Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing; [Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optim\n \n ## Checklist\n \n+- [ ] Sign off every non-merge commit with `git commit -s` to certify the [Developer Certificate of Origin](https://developercertificate.org/).\n - [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n - [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n - [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/bf2d469148d1639816b0ac076fe8e9e19ddab34e/.github%2Fpull_request_template.md",
      "sha": "d8b70af52ec16371eafe5901d1b012e070806aec",
      "status": "modified"
